# Wopal Plugin — Environment Configuration
# Copy this file to $WOPAL_HOME/.env or <space>/.wopal/.env and fill in your values.
#
# This file carries connection parameters, secrets, and log diagnostics overrides.
# Feature configuration (module switches) lives in the top-level `wopal` node of
# settings.jsonc (see docs/DESIGN-wopal-plugin.md §5.3 / §5.4), not in environment
# variables. Endpoint/model settings may also live in the `wopal` config node;
# config values take precedence over the environment variables below.
#
# Loading order (higher priority overrides lower):
#   1. process.env (pre-existing, never overwritten)
#   2. <space>/.wopal/.env (space-level)
#   3. $WOPAL_HOME/.env (user-level, shared across spaces)
# Only the variables listed below are loaded; all other WOPAL_* variables are ignored.

# ─── LLM connection ───

# LLM API endpoint (REQUIRED when not set in the wopal config node)
# WOPAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Model name (optional, defaults to gpt-4o-mini)
# WOPAL_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# API key for the LLM service (REQUIRED when not set in the wopal config node;
# may also be referenced from settings.jsonc as "apiKey": "$WOPAL_LLM_API_KEY")
# WOPAL_LLM_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# ─── Embedding connection ───

# Embedding API endpoint (REQUIRED when not set in the wopal config node)
# WOPAL_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Embedding model name (REQUIRED when not set in the wopal config node)
# WOPAL_EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# API key for the embedding service (optional for local servers)
# WOPAL_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here

# ─── Logging diagnostics ───

# Log level: trace | debug | info | warn | error | fatal (default: info)
# WOPAL_PLUGIN_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Module filter: comma-separated (core | rules | task | memory | context), empty = all
# WOPAL_PLUGIN_LOG_MODULES=

# Log file path (default: $WOPAL_HOME/logs/wopal-plugin.log)
# WOPAL_PLUGIN_LOG_FILE=
